$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: tert-butyl
5-((14Z)-1-(5-formyl-3,4-dihydro-4,4-dimethylpyrrol-2-
ylidene)ethyl)-3,4-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole-2-carboxylate (12a). A solution of
21a (717 mg, 2.17 mmol) in DMF (20 mL) and pyridine (210 μL, 2.60 mmol)
was treated with SeO2 (289 mg, 2.60 mmol) and stirred at rt for 5 h. The
reaction was then heated to 80°C for 15 min. The reaction mixture was
cooled to rt, filtered, and poured into water. The solution was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL), and the combined organic extracts were washed
sequentially with saturated aq NaHCO3 and brine, dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated. The resulting oil was purified by flash
chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc:hexanes = 3:7) to give 12a (483 mg,
65%) as an orange crystalline solid. tert-butyl
5-((14Z)-(5-formyl-3,4-dihydro-4,4-dimethylpyrrol-2-ylidene)-
methyl)-3,4-dimethyl-1H-pyrrole-2-carboxylate (12c). Following the
procedure outlined for 12a, reaction of 21c (1.15 g, 3.63 mmol) with SeO2
(484 mg, 4.36 mmol) in DMF (20 mL) and pyridine (350 μL, 4.36 mmol) gave
12c (850 mg, 71%) as an orange crystalline solid, decomp. > 131.8°C. R f
(1:4 EtOAc/hexanes) 0.55; IR(thin film) 1689, 1456, 1252, 1174, 1143
cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.36 (s, 6H), 1.59 (s, 9H), 2.05 (s, 3H),
2.26 (s, 3H), 2.74 (s, 2H), 6.26 (s, 1H), 9.93 (s, 1H), 10.78 (br s, 1H);
13C NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.1, 10.4, 25.8, 28.7, 46.46, 46.50, 80.7,
113.3, 122.6, 122.7, 126.3, 129.7, 150.9, 161.0, 177.7, 190.4. Anal.
