$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Oxidation of indazolones Ia-If (general
procedure). Water, 1.5 mmol (0.03 g, 0.03 ml), was added to 1.5 mmol
(0.17 g) of finely powdered selenium(IV) oxide, 3 mmol (0.29 g, 0.16 ml)
of concentrated sulfuric acid was added, the mixture was stirred for 20
min, and a solution of 1 mmol of indazolone Ia-If in 10 ml of glacial
acetic acid was added to the resulting suspension. The mixture was left
to stand for 5 days at room temperature with intermittent shaking. It was
then treated with a mixture of 40 ml of 25% aqueous ammonia and 20 g of
ice and extracted with chloroform (3 × 20 ml), the organic phase was
separated, dried over anhydrous MgSO4, and filtered, the solvent was
removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was subjected to column
chromatography to isolate indazole-4,5-diones IIa-IIf.
6,6-Dimethyl-3-perfluoropropyl-1-phenyl-6,7-dihydro-1H-indazole-4,5-dione
(IIc). Yield 71%, colorless crystalline substance. mp 39-42°C. IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1705, 1695, 1500. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.33 s (6H,
CH3), 3.21 s (2H, 7-H), 7.52-7.61 m (5H, Harom). 13C NMR spectrum, δC,
ppm: 24.5 (6-CH3), 36.4 (C6), 45.9 (C7), 108.9 t.m (CF3CF2, 1JCF = 266
Hz), 112.6 t.t (3-CF2, 1JCF = 255 Hz, 2JCF = 32), 118.0 q.t (CF3, 1JCF =
288 Hz, 2JCF = 34 Hz), 119.3 (C3a), 124.6 (Carom), 130.0 (Carom), 130.1
(Carom), 137.1 (Carom), 140.6 t (C3, 2JCF = 31 Hz), 149.6 (C7a), 173.8
(C4), 199.1 (C5). 19F NMR spectrum, δF, ppm: -80.4 (CF3), -110.2 (CF2),
-126.0 (CF2). Found, %: C 51.26; H 3.15; N 6.69. C18H13F7N2O2.
Calculated, %: C 51.19; H 3.10; N 6.63.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of perfluoroalkyl-substituted
4,5-dihydro-3H-pyrazolo[4,3-a]phenazines and
tetrahydroimidazo[4,5-e]indazoles
