$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of (E)-Ethyl
4-[2-methyl-1-(phenylsulfonyl)-1H-indol-3-yl]-4-oxobut-2-enoate 4k SeO2
(797 mg, 7.1 mmol) was added to a solution of
1-phenylsulfonyl-2-methyl-3-acetylindole (1.5 g, 4.7 mmol) in dioxane
(40mL) and refluxed for 10 h. The resulting reaction mixture was passed
over a Celite pad and washed with DCM (2 x 15 mL). The combined extracts
were washed with H2O (2x25mL). Removal of solvent afforded
2-[2-methyl-1-(phenylsulfonyl)-1H-indol-3-yl]-2-oxoacetaldehyde (1.09g,
70%), 2-[2-methyl-1-(phenylsulfonyl)-1H-indol-3-yl]-2-oxoacetaldehyde,
yield (1.09g, 70%).
