$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-[(5-Formyl-4,4-dimethyl-3,4-dihydro-pyrrol-2-ylidene)-phenyl-methyl]-3,4-dimethyl-1Hpyrrole-2-carbaldehyde
(6a). A solution of 13a (244 mg, 0.727 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (15 mL) and
pyridine (59 μL, 0.73 mmol) was treated with SeO2 (83.3 mg, 0.727 mmol)
and stirred at rt for 5 h. The solvent was then removed by rotary
evaporation, and the residue was redissolved in DMF (10 mL) and heated to
80°C for 15 min. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt, filtered, and
poured into water (50 mL). The solution was extracted with CH2Cl2 (4 × 20
mL), and the combined organic extracts were washed sequentially with
saturated aq NaHCO3 and brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The resulting oil was purified by flash chromatography
(silica gel, EtOAc:hexanes = 3:7) to give 6a (170 mg, 70%) as an orange
crystalline solid
5-[(5-Formyl-4,4-dimethyl-3,4-dihydro-pyrrol-2-ylidene)-phenyl-methyl]-3,4-dimethyl-1Hpyrrole-2-carbaldehyde
(6a), Yield (170 mg, 70%) mp 169.8-170.6°C. Rf (1:4 EtOAc/hexanes) 0.19;
IR(thin film) 3321, 1688, 1629, 1442, 1311, 1182 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 1.28 (s, 3H), 1.31 (s, 6H), 2.22 (s, 3H), 2.54 (s, 2H), 7.25-
7.46 (m, 5H), 9.70 (s, 1H), 10.03 (s, 1H), 11.05 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.9, 10.2, 25.8, 46.4, 46.8, 123.7, 128.5, 129.2, 129.3,
130.2, 130.4, 131.4, 134.2, 138.8, 153.1, 177.6, 178.9, 190.7. Anal.
Calcd for C21H22N2O2: C, 75.42; H, 6.63; N, 8.38; O, 9.57. Found: C,
75.21; H, 6.70; N, 8.39.1
