$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 15 (25 g, 0.11 mol) in CH2Cl2 (150 mL) was added SeO2
(24 g, 0.22 mol) and AcOH (50 mL). The suspension was refluxed at 60 °C
for 48 h. The mixture was cooled to room temperature, diluted with ether
and filtered. The filtrate was washed with 3N KOH and concentrated. The
crude product was chromatographed on silica gel (hexanes:Et2O = 3:1→
hexanes:EtOAc = 2:1) to give 16 (1.9 g, 8%) and alcohol S2 (20 g, 79%).
16, yield (1.9 g, 8%); S2, yield (20 g, 79%). For 16, Rf = 0.37 (silica,
25% EtOAc in hexanes);1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 9.38 (s, 1H), 6.69 (m,
1H), 4.98 (d, J = 5 Hz, 1H), 3.39 (ABq, J = 67.5, 10 Hz, 2H), 2.96 (m,
1H), 2.66 (m, 1H), 2.48 (br t, 1H), 2.45 (dt, J = 11.5, 5 Hz, 2H), 1.78
(d, J = 11 Hz, 1H), 1.40 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 190.4,
149.4, 146.0, 85.4, 68.3, 40.7, 37.8, 33.9, 31.0, 26.0; IR (thin film):
νmax = 2977, 2844, 1670, 1374, 1005 cm-1; [α]D29 = 85.8 (c = 0.5, CHCl3);
HRMS (m/z ): [M]+ calcd for C10H13O2Br 244.0098, found 244.0095. For S2,
Rf = 0.15 (silica, 35% EtOAc in hexanes);1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 5.52
(m, 1H), 4.31 (d, J = 5 Hz, 1H), 4.00 (s, 1H), 3.42 (ABq, J = 10, 3.5 Hz,
2H), 2.55 (m, 1H), 2.44 (s, 1H), 2.36 - 2.29 (m, 3H), 1.89 (d, J = 11 Hz,
1H), 1.36 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 143.1, 122.5, 83.0, 73.7,
64.4, 40.8, 38.5, 34.6, 29.3, 26.2; IR (neat): νmax = 3377, 2955, 1652,
1449, 1024 cm-1; [α]D29 = 26.5 (c = 0.5, CHCl3); HRMS (m/z ): [M]+ calcd
for C10H15O2Br 246.0255, found 246.0255.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
